This is the Bracket 4 version of Sisay for one reason: it destroys everybody's lands. Living Plane turns every land on the table into a creature, and Elesh Norn gives your creatures +2/+2 while giving theirs -2/-2 — so their entire mana base dies and yours grows. Mass land denial is not legal below Bracket 4, and it is the whole point of the build. Everything else is a tutor chain that assembles those two cards.

# The lock
Living Plane :: all lands are 1/1 creatures. On its own it does nothing; it is half of a one-sided Armageddon.
Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite :: your other creatures get +2/+2 and theirs get -2/-2. With any land animation out, every land your opponents control is a 1/1 or 2/2 taking -2/-2 — it dies immediately, and yours become 3/3s.
Nature's Revolt :: the second copy of the animation, at 2/2.
Natural Affinity :: the INSTANT-speed version. Hold it with Elesh Norn already on the battlefield and wipe the table's mana at the end of somebody's turn, or in response to removal aimed at Norn.
Kudo, King Among Bears :: sets other creatures to base 2/2, which turns on the same interaction and shrinks every fatty at the table on the way.
Be deliberate about this. It ends games and it is miserable to sit through. Deploy it when you can actually close, not on turn five for value.

# The commander, and untapping her
Captain Sisay :: {T} to search out ANY legendary card — creature, land, artifact, enchantment or planeswalker — straight to your hand. Elesh Norn is legendary; most of the lock's protection is too.
Instill Energy :: {0} to untap her once per turn, and it grants haste. Two tutors a turn from a one-mana Aura.
Thousand-Year Elixir :: haste for the activation plus a separate untap.
Sting, the Glinting Dagger :: haste and a free untap at the beginning of each combat.
Seedborn Muse :: untaps everything on all three opponents' turns. Four Sisay activations per round.
Lightning Greaves :: haste the turn she lands, and shroud against the removal that follows.
Sigarda, Font of Blessings :: your other permanents get hexproof, which covers Sisay and the enchantments.
Sterling Grove :: shroud for your other enchantments, and it sacrifices to tutor one.

# The other tutors
Idyllic Tutor :: any enchantment — Living Plane, Nature's Revolt, Survival of the Fittest.
Moon-Blessed Cleric :: the same on a body.
Enlightened Tutor :: instant speed, to the top.
Worldly Tutor :: any creature, to the top.
Eladamri's Call :: any creature, to hand, at instant speed.
Recruiter of the Guard :: any creature with toughness 2 or less.
Ranger-Captain of Eos :: a one-drop, and it sacrifices to stop every noncreature spell for a turn.
Green Sun's Zenith :: any green creature onto the battlefield.
Chord of Calling :: instant speed, convoke.
Finale of Devastation :: library or graveyard, and at X of ten it is the kill.
Eldritch Evolution :: turns a spent mana dork into a five-drop.
Survival of the Fittest :: the engine — a green mana and a spare creature finds any creature in the deck, repeatedly.
Pattern of Rebirth :: on any creature, its death fetches anything. With a sacrifice outlet it is a tutor for Elesh Norn.
Academy Rector :: dies into ANY enchantment onto the battlefield — Living Plane, for free.
Defense of the Heart :: two creatures from your library onto the battlefield, which is Elesh Norn plus whatever ends the game.
Loyal Retainers :: returns a legendary creature from the graveyard, which is a second Elesh Norn after a wrath.

# Protecting the turn
Grand Abolisher :: they cannot cast spells or activate abilities during your turn at all.
Jennifer Walters :: the same lockout on a body that later flips into a 6/6.
Silence :: one mana, and nobody interacts for a turn.
Boromir, Warden of the Tower :: counters anything cast for free, and sacrifices to make your board indestructible.
Linvala, Keeper of Silence :: their creature abilities all stop — including the mana dorks they were going to rebuild with.
Flawless Maneuver :: free with a commander out.
Heroic Intervention :: hexproof and indestructible for everything.
Veil of Summer :: one mana against blue and black.
Legolas's Quick Reflexes :: split second, so it protects Sisay through anything, and it untaps her.
Destiny Spinner :: your creature and enchantment spells cannot be countered.
Force of Vigor :: free on their turn, destroying two artifacts or enchantments.
Swords to Plowshares :: the cleanest removal in the format.

# Mana
Birds of Paradise :: turn-one fixing.
Llanowar Elves :: the green half.
Elvish Mystic :: the second copy.
Fyndhorn Elves :: the third.
Avacyn's Pilgrim :: the white one.
Arbor Elf :: untaps a Forest, and with Wild Growth or Utopia Sprawl on it that is two or three mana.
Wild Growth :: the aura that makes Arbor Elf a ritual.
Utopia Sprawl :: the same, with fixing.
Bloom Tender :: two colours off one tap.
Delighted Halfling :: uncounterable mana for legendary spells, which is most of the deck.
Selvala, Heart of the Wilds :: mana equal to your biggest creature, which after Elesh Norn is a lot.
Badgermole Cub :: an extra green for every creature tapped for mana.
Sol Ring :: the fastest start.
Mana Vault :: three on turn one.
Lotus Petal :: free acceleration.
Mox Amber :: live from the moment any legend resolves.
Mox Diamond :: a land for a Mox.
Chrome Mox :: fast, at the cost of a card.
Elvish Spirit Guide :: a free green from hand.
Crop Rotation :: any land onto the battlefield at instant speed.

# Closing after the lock
Kamahl, Fist of Krosa :: animates lands and pumps the team +3/+3 with trample. With Living Plane already out, your lands are the army.
Concordant Crossroads :: everything has haste, so the turn you assemble the lock is the turn you attack.
Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite :: the +2/+2 half is a real clock on a board of legends.
Finale of Devastation :: at X of ten, a tutor and lethal in one card.
The One Ring :: a turn of protection and then the cards to rebuild.
Sylvan Library :: with this much tutoring, the four-life payments are almost always right.
Esper Sentinel :: taxes their first noncreature spell each turn.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep a mana dork and a tutor. Turn-one acceleration into a turn-two or three Sisay is what makes the lock arrive before anyone can set up.
Assemble the animation and Elesh Norn in the SAME turn where possible. Living Plane on its own telegraphs everything and invites the enchantment removal that ruins the plan.
Natural Affinity is the surprise version. With Elesh Norn already down, holding three mana means you can wipe the table's lands at instant speed — usually at the end of the turn before yours.
Sisay finds lands too. Do not forget the legendary lands in your own mana base; against a table with no pressure, fetching a utility land is often better than a threat.
